{"title":"2025 WSMO Accuracy Round Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79058441b6eb9b985c3f36dcf8250860da926bdd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x+y=10\\quad\\text{ and }\\quad x^2+y^2=58.\\]\" width=\"258\" height=\"19\" /> Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/2/e526fbac5ee18e20a7293e9cb9c317989b31988a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x-y|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 WSMO Accuracy Round Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/164abb6bd18d06bfe942472fac852a1df64b2f0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/5/ed5b731584178873633d009c87934de1cfb6d38f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/f/7efc8d80a7212548e17ed6cab5fe464084d0e9d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = 34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/2/ba2685a963feb8454715e65aa77baf6d2c0a2c4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = 25$\" width=\"72\" height=\"12\" />. Find the minimum possible length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d9456e0361813641f4ce80980839e9038fe8f7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 WSMO Accuracy Round Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On a string of holiday lights, there are 4 blue lights for every 3 green lights, 7 red lights for every 6 blue lights, and 20 white lights for every 13 colored lights. What is the smallest number of lights that can be on the string of lights?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 WSMO Accuracy Round Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Evaluate: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/9/19978447d13680111bb3f830c089800c96e3bf17.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{1 \\le a,b \\le 25} \\left \\lfloor \\frac{a+b\\sqrt{2}}{1+\\sqrt{2}} \\right \\rfloor.\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 WSMO Accuracy Round Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba7523871b75e706db0c5df71ee517480937e0ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> be an ellipse. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> lie on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba7523871b75e706db0c5df71ee517480937e0ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/4/854bf4459317b2ed4a2d3ff5a6a243ff01d50274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WY$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bb2419be49ff83cbed7db9a2f366858ccabf2e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XZ$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> are parallel to the minor and major axes of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba7523871b75e706db0c5df71ee517480937e0ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" />, respectively. Suppose that segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/4/854bf4459317b2ed4a2d3ff5a6a243ff01d50274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WY$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bb2419be49ff83cbed7db9a2f366858ccabf2e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XZ$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> intersect at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/1/8015c2469662484bcce9be16982856ce77facdad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PW = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/e/55ef02ae632238ef4ad0d8e27cb569914c9f089a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/b/29bcddafe3f9b88c03d04020b2bdc956f6cbbdfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PY = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/6/6761848274bffd08d45a864f61df3d930917fe38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PZ = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba7523871b75e706db0c5df71ee517480937e0ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/8/f2800c97a993fcdb732028a419d6d19a74cbc64c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\pi$\" width=\"21\" height=\"8\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 WSMO Accuracy Round Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/9/2398fea7844af8851455a88fadca5359597ad8a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1, t_2, \\dots, t_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" /> be integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/2/5d221cf45d8ecb007aa1efc310b6050eaf8e976a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N &lt; 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"15\" /> be a positive integer such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/242c9723a94857215975b06f6a93d3cfc37165ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Nt_1 &lt; 60t_2 &lt; 27t_3 &lt; 8t_4 &lt; 50t_5 &lt; 45t_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"306\" height=\"17\" />. Over all choices of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/9/2398fea7844af8851455a88fadca5359597ad8a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1, t_2, \\dots, t_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />, the minimum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/c/09cd32969ceb9c6025809746dc68248b8e801bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45t_6 - Nt_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Find the sum of all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 WSMO Accuracy Round Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of all non-congruent right triangles with integer side lengths such that the area of the triangle is equal to three times the perimeter of the triangle. Find the sum of the lengths of hypotenuses of all the right triangles in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 WSMO Accuracy Round Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Nonnegative real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> satisfy the system of equations \n\\begin{align*}\n16x^6-24x^4+9x^2&amp;=\\frac{y+1}{2}\\\\\n8y^3-6y&amp;=1.\n\\end{align*}\nThe smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/f/b7f01dc25316aabc98646f32202a2d3da0803ee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\arccos(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62fabf626cac8c34e8886029cce2d7cfa2fde87e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}^{\\circ},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"34\" height=\"36\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 WSMO Accuracy Round Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Amy the ant lives in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc9bcf76cf936718b266bc4ea68b525ea852df68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\times2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> rectangular grid of dots shown. From some dot <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79a4f97ce27c2bb251b589501c8f83b8d33612b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{D}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" />, she can move to a dot that is either horizontally adjacent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79a4f97ce27c2bb251b589501c8f83b8d33612b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{D}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" />, diagonally adjacent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79a4f97ce27c2bb251b589501c8f83b8d33612b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{D}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" />, or connected to D by a segment. In how many different ways can Amy visit every dot exactly once if she starts at the starred dot?\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/2/cf29de6056d17a5ef9e83fd312878967593f9566.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(5cm); import geometry;  point P1=(1,1); point P2=(2,1); point P3=(3,1); point P4=(4,1); point P5=(5,1); point P6=(6,1); point P13=(7,1); point P15=(8,1); point P7=(1,2); point P8=(2,2); point P9=(3,2); point P10=(4,2); point P11=(5,2); point P12=(6,2); point P14=(7,2); point P16=(8,2);  draw(P15--P16);  dot(P1); dot(P2); dot(P3); dot(P4); dot(P5); dot(P6); dot(P7); dot(P8); dot(P9); dot(P10); dot(P11); dot(P12); dot(P13); dot(P14); dot(P15); dot(P16);  label(&quot;$\\star$&quot;,P1,dir(-135)); [/asy]\" width=\"238\" height=\"52\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 WSMO Accuracy Round Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d59e6b371eb2a3206d9ec376adadd2beb3c34f64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:\\{1,2,\\dots,20\\} \\to \\{1,2,\\dots,20\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"262\" height=\"20\" /> be a function such that for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c27fb46cb4fb2915e95133d1ca99356e8667416.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m,n \\in \\{1,2,\\dots, 20\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"162\" height=\"20\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/5/ed50f56dee7b1b790a7fa12651ed28f92641161e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\gcd(m,f(n)) = \\gcd(n,f(m)).\\]\" width=\"229\" height=\"18\" /> How many such functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> are there?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2025 WSMO Accuracy Round Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018070915\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.040 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 325/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10696/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35275:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018070915 and revision id 273695. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}